1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,240
A market scan is not just a list of tickers.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:06,803
It is a definition of what the research can actually trust.

3
00:00:06,803 --> 00:00:08,874
Start with the asset catalogue.

4
00:00:08,874 --> 00:00:14,672
Confirm the instrument class, listing venue, current status and whether it is tradable through

5
00:00:14,672 --> 00:00:17,158
the route you intend to use.

6
00:00:17,158 --> 00:00:21,713
Data availability and execution availability are not always the same thing.

7
00:00:21,713 --> 00:00:24,743
Then separate instruments that answer different questions.

8
00:00:24,743 --> 00:00:30,801
A common share is not an exchange-traded fund, a warrant or a preferred security.

9
00:00:30,801 --> 00:00:34,696
A wrapper can carry a different structure and risk.

10
00:00:34,696 --> 00:00:40,755
The SEC notes that leveraged and inverse ETFs are designed around daily objectives, so

11
00:00:40,755 --> 00:00:44,217
longer-period results can diverge from the underlying benchmark.

12
00:00:44,217 --> 00:00:47,085
Next, test whether the quote is usable.

13
00:00:47,085 --> 00:00:53,642
A wide bid-ask spread, thin activity or inconsistent volume can make a screen price look more

14
00:00:53,642 --> 00:00:56,100
precise than the market really is.

15
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:59,379
Liquidity is part of data quality, not decoration.

16
00:00:59,379 --> 00:01:01,115
Check the history too.

17
00:01:01,115 --> 00:01:06,756
Missing sessions, abrupt symbol changes or too few completed observations can distort averages

18
00:01:06,756 --> 00:01:08,058
and momentum measures.

19
00:01:08,058 --> 00:01:15,002
Keep the timestamp with every bar, and make sure the interval has actually closed before using

20
00:01:15,002 --> 00:01:16,304
its final value.

21
00:01:16,304 --> 00:01:21,935
Now define the boundaries: which exchanges, which instrument types, what data feeds and what

22
00:01:21,935 --> 00:01:23,544
regions are genuinely connected.

23
00:01:23,544 --> 00:01:27,566
If a market is not connected, label it that way.

24
00:01:27,566 --> 00:01:32,392
Do not let a broad-looking watchlist imply coverage you do not have.

25
00:01:32,392 --> 00:01:37,158
Only after those checks should a candidate enter a research ranking.

26
00:01:37,158 --> 00:01:43,223
A clean universe does not predict a return and does not create a recommendation.

27
00:01:43,223 --> 00:01:49,722
It simply makes the next question more honest: is the evidence complete enough to continue?

28
00:01:49,722 --> 00:01:54,487
Paper-trading education only; not live-money performance; not investment advice; no guaranteed

29
00:01:54,487 --> 00:01:54,921
returns.
